#: src/dcc-gui.c:10407
msgid "Switch on direct EC access?"
msgstr ""

#: src/dcc-gui.c:10409
msgid ""
"<b>This can damage your laptop.</b> The fan daemon would then write directly "
"to the Embedded Controller through the I/O ports 0x62/0x66, using the "
"register layout of Clevo laptops. On a laptop with a different layout, these "
"writes can change charging, power or thermal settings, stop the fans or "
"overheat the hardware.\n"
"\n"
"Only use it on a Clevo-based laptop where the dcc_fan module does not load. "
"Before the first write, the daemon checks that the EC answers like a Clevo "
"EC and refuses otherwise, but this check cannot rule out every risk.\n"
"\n"
"You use it at your own risk."
msgstr ""

#: src/dcc-gui.c:10417 src/dcc-gui.c:10495
msgid "Switch on"
msgstr ""

#: src/dcc-gui.c:10420
msgid "I understand the risk and use this on a Clevo-based laptop"
msgstr ""

#: src/dcc-gui.c:10425
msgid "Direct EC access"
msgstr ""

#: src/dcc-gui.c:10488
msgid "Switch on generic fan control?"
msgstr ""

#: src/dcc-gui.c:10490
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The fan daemon then sets the speed of the %s driver's fans through the "
"kernel's standard interface, following your fan profiles. Only fans whose "
"driver offers a manual mode are used.\n"
"\n"
"If the fan daemon stops, the fans run at 100%% until it starts again or the "
"laptop restarts. Switched off, the fans go back to the driver's automatic "
"mode."
msgstr ""

